cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or benchmark, please cite it as below."
title: "Finite-Data Stress Tests for Spectral Causal Emergence"
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-14
type: software
license: "MIT"
authors:
  - given-names: "Sergi"
    family-names: "Garcia Mecinas"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible benchmark examining what finite transition data can support
  about spectral and rank-based causal-emergence claims. The benchmark studies
  representation sensitivity, finite-sample rank fragility, forced spectral
  cutoff behavior, conservative one-sided resolved-mode inference, and exact
  triadic controls separating spectral rank from macro-partition validity.
keywords:
  - causal emergence
  - complex systems
  - Markov chains
  - singular value decomposition
  - spectral analysis
  - finite-sample inference
  - effective information
  - reproducible research
  - lumpability
  - macrostate discovery
repository-code: "https://github.com/sgarcia87/finite-data-causal-emergence-stress-test"
url: "https://github.com/sgarcia87/finite-data-causal-emergence-stress-test"
